                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Technical state is really bad for a game that is sold officially on steam in 2026, the fact that game launches doesn't make it automatically playble, verified and etc.\r\n\r\nNetcode doesn't work, game crashes freqeuntly cause memory leak, playing in online coop is a torture for second player. Once again players do more for technical support of old games than devs and publishers that  make money, fan fix on github Tervel1337/KL2Fix tries to fix some problems, but its still doesn't fix netcode. Stop killing games is not enough, there should Stop selling technical mess that pretends to work on modern systems\r\n\r\nOtherwise unique art direction, unique sound design, worth to be experienced. There should be more experiments like this in gamedev",
